#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# product_log

#% text
# `product_log(z)` gives the principal branch of the Lambert W function, the solution w of w e^w = z.

#% text
# `product_log(k, z)` gives branch k.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# Exact values at 0, e and -1/e; machine numbers (real and complex) by Halley's iteration.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
product_log(1.0)
#% output
#= 0.5671432904097838

#% cell
product_log(e)
#% output
#= 1

#% cell
product_log(-1, -0.2)
#% output
#= -2.5426413577735265

#% subsection
# Scope

#% cell
product_log(2.0*im)
#% output
#= complex(0.683408016326576, 0.743386004741352)

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `exp`, `log`
